id\" : \"node-design-claude_design-008\",\n  \"handler_type\" : \"acpx.agent_run\",\n  \"decision\" : \"READY_FOR_ARCH_REVIEW\",\n  \"summary\" : \"以两步 str.replace 纯函数实现 normalize_newlines，用 11 个 unittest 用例覆盖 AC-1 全部九类输入与幂等性，并以 doctest 可验证的 README 示例覆盖 AC-3。\",\n  \"required_keys\" : [ \"summary\", \"decision\" ],\n  \"allowed_decisions\" : [ \"READY_FOR_ARCH_REVIEW\" ],\n  \"source_output_ref\" : \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261023T005431Z-9YYF/runs/run-1792718401135/outputs/design-claude.json\",\n  \"source_artifact_type\" : \"design_result\",\n  \"generated_at\" : \"2026-10-23T01:23:30.274231Z\",\n  \"control\" : {\n    \"decision\" : \"READY_FOR_ARCH_REVIEW\",\n    \"summary\" : \"以两步 str.replace 纯函数实现 normalize_newlines，用 11 个 unittest 用例覆盖 AC-1 全部九类输入与幂等性，并以 doctest 可验证的 README 示例覆盖 AC-3。\"\n  },\n  \"control_source\" : {\n    \"kind\" : \"strict_agent_result_envelope\"\n  },\n  \"revision_responses\" : [ ],\n  \"lifecycle_status\" : \"READY\",\n  \"checks\" : [ \"已实际读取已批准的 TaskContract（contract-resolution.md 显示 Decision: APPROVE，由 human_gate 于 2026-10-23T01:19:39Z 批准），设计目标、Scope 排除项、Constraints 与 Non-Goals 与契约逐条对齐。\", \"已用 Glob 核对仓库现状：src/ 与 tests/ 目录不存在，仓库根无 README.md 与任何源码文件（repo-map fileCount=0），故三个计划文件均为 CREATE；不创建或修改 .git/ 与 .agent/ 下的任何文件。\", \"语义边界与契约 Constraints 精确一致：仅将每个 \\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\" 与孤立 \\\"\\\\r\\\" 转为 \\\"\\\\n\\\"；空串返回空串、已有 LF 原样保留、Unicode 字符（含 U+2028/U+2029）不变、末尾有/无换行状态原样保留（不新增、不删除）；纯函数且重复调用幂等。\", \"替换顺序不变量已定：必须先 text.replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\") 再 text.replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\")，否则 CRLF 会被拆成两个 LF；由 test_crlf_becomes_single_lf 显式断言 \\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\" 结果为 \\\"a\\\\nb\\\" 而非 \\\"a\\\\n\\\\nb\\\"。\", \"导入机制已按契约 Risk Areas 要求在设计中定案并留待 EXECUTION 计划确认：测试文件顶部用 pathlib 将仓库 src/ 插入 sys.path，使 python -m unittest discover -s tests -v 从仓库根目录可实际执行；不新增 pyproject.toml、requirements.txt 或 __init__.py（Non-Goal 明确排除依赖清单与打包发布）。\", \"状态与生命周期边界声明：本设计不新增索引、锁、事务、队列、缓存、外部副作用或补偿机制，函数为无状态纯函数且无 I/O，故并发、超时/提供方失败、中断/崩溃、重启/恢复、回滚/冲突及 cannot-bypass 各边界均不适用，无需为其设计防护或测试。\", \"AC-2 证据形态已约束：EXECUTION 阶段在仓库根实际执行 python -m unittest discover -s tests -v 并原样保留 stdout（逐用例名、Ran 11 tests、OK），输出用例与测试源码一一对应；不以“测试已完成”之类的完成状态或文字结论替代实际输入/输出。\", \"AC-3 验证途径已约束：实际读取 src/normalize_text.py 与 README.md 比对导入语句与逐字符输出，或实际执行 PYTHONPATH=src python -m doctest README.md（TR-3 允许任一途径）。\" ],\n  \"evidence\" : [ \"契约依据：.agent/workstreams/ws-20261023T005431Z-9YYF/artifacts/contracts/node-contract-compile-007/task-contract.md 的 Objective、Scope、Acceptance Criteria、Test Requirements、Constraints、Non-Goals、Risk Areas 均已读取并映射到本设计。\", \"仓库现状实测：Glob 模式 {src,tests}/** 无匹配，仓库可见文件仅位于 .git 与 .agent 之下，故 planned_files 三项均为新建（CREATE），不覆盖任何现有文件。\", \"AC-1 覆盖依据：测试模块顶部定义共享 CASES 表，九类输入各有精确期望——\\\"\\\"→\\\"\\\"；\\\"a\\\\nb\\\\n\\\"→\\\"a\\\\nb\\\\n\\\"；\\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\"→\\\"a\\\\nb\\\"；\\\"a\\\\rb\\\"→\\\"a\\\\nb\\\"；\\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\\rc\\\\nd\\\"→\\\"a\\\\n\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\nd\\\"；\\\"中文\\\\u2028😀\\\\r\\\\nx\\\"→\\\"中文\\\\u2028😀\\\\nx\\\"（U+2028 保留不转换）；\\\"end\\\\r\\\\n\\\"→\\\"end\\\\n\\\"；\\\"no newline\\\"→\\\"no newline\\\"；\\\"a\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\rb\\\"→\\\"a\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nb\\\"；再由 test_idempotent_across_all_cases 以 subTest 遍历同一张表断言 normalize_newlines(normalize_newlines(x)) == normalize_newlines(x)（输出不含 CR，二次调用为恒等映射）。\", \"测试结构依据：11 个测试方法——test_empty_string_returns_empty、test_pure_lf_unchanged、test_crlf_becomes_single_lf、test_lone_cr_becomes_lf、test_mixed_newlines_normalized、test_unicode_and_line_separators_preserved、test_trailing_newline_present_kept、test_trailing_newline_absent_kept、test_consecutive_blank_lines_normalized、test_no_cr_left_in_output、test_idempotent_across_all_cases——方法名与 verbose 输出逐条对应，使 AC-2 的“输出所列用例与测试源码相符”可直接核对；末尾孤立 CR（\\\"a\\\\r\\\"→\\\"a\\\\n\\\"）归入末尾有换行类：CR 本身是换行，仅重编码为 LF，换行存在性保持。\", \"实现依据：两步 replace 为标准库 str 方法，语义无歧义；错误顺序可证伪——\\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\".replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\") == \\\"a\\\\n\\\\nb\\\"，正确顺序 replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\").replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\",\\\"\\\\n\\\") == \\\"a\\\\nb\\\"，该对比构成顺序断言的期望依据。\", \"AC-3 依据：README 示例采用 doctest 风格、单行 repr 输出（>>> from normalize_text import normalize_newlines；>>> normalize_newlines(\\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\\rc\\\\nd\\\") 期望 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\nd'，另含空串与末尾换行示例），与实现逐字符一致且可被 python -m doctest README.md 实际执行。\", \"AC-2 依据：unittest discover 的 verbose 模式输出每个用例名并以 Ran 11 tests 与 OK 结束，天然呈现覆盖数与零 failure/error，满足 TR-2 对真实命令输出（而非转述）的要求。\" ],\n  \"missing_evidence\" : [ ],\n  \"must_fix\" : [ ],\n  \"open_risks\" : [ \"src 布局的导入依赖测试文件内 sys.path 注入（或运行时 PYTHONPATH=src）：该机制是契约 Risk Areas 指定的 EXECUTION 计划确认项，若计划评审改为包结构或平铺布局，需同步调整 README 的导入说明（仍在同一批准文件集内解决）。\", \"Ran 11 tests 中的 11 对应当前设计的测试方法数：若计划或实现阶段增删用例，须同步更新 README/执行记录中的用例数与用例对应关系，避免 AC-2 覆盖数与测试源码不符。\" ],\n  \"verification_summary\" : \"仅完成设计与方案核对（读取契约、决议与仓库现状）；未编写代码、未执行测试、未创建或修改任何仓库文件。\",\n  \"design\" : {\n    \"planned_files\" : [ {\n      \"responsibility\" : \"实现 normalize_newlines(text: str) -> str：先 text.replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\") 再 text.replace(\\\"\\\\r\\\", \\\"\\\\n\\\")，将 CRLF 与孤立 CR 转为 LF；空串、已有 LF、Unicode 字符（含 U+2028/U+2029）与末尾换行有无全部原样保留；纯函数、仅标准库、无 I/O、无状态、无外部副作用。\",\n      \"path\" : \"src/normalize_text.py\",\n      \"operation\" : \"CREATE\"\n    }, {\n      \"responsibility\" : \"unittest 测试：文件顶部以 pathlib 将仓库 src/ 目录插入 sys.path 以支持从仓库根执行 python -m unittest discover -s tests -v；定义覆盖九类输入（空串、纯 LF、CRLF、单 CR、混合换行、Unicode、末尾有换行、末尾无换行、连续空行）精确期望的共享 CASES 表，共 11 个测试方法，含 CRLF 不拆为双 LF 的替换顺序断言、输出无残留 CR 的全局断言、以及以 subTest 遍历 CASES 的幂等性断言。\",\n      \"path\" : \"tests/test_normalize_text.py\",\n      \"operation\" : \"CREATE\"\n    }, {\n      \"responsibility\" : \"中文用法文档：函数语义规则（含不转换 U+2028/U+2029、不新增或删除末尾换行）、导入方式（PYTHONPATH=src 或与测试一致的 sys.path 做法）、doctest 风格示例（含 from normalize_text import normalize_newlines 导入语句与 \\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\\rc\\\\nd\\\" → 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\nd' 的典型混合换行输入/输出）、以及 python -m unittest discover -s tests -v 运行测试命令；示例与 src/normalize_text.py 实现逐字符一致。\",\n      \"path\" : \"README.md\",\n      \"operation\" : \"CREATE\"\n    } ]\n  },\n  \"stage_outcome\" : \"READY\",\n  \"stage_outcome_source\" : \"declared_status\",\n  \"evidence_state\" : {\n    \"blocking\" : false,\n    \"evidence_count\" : 7,\n    \"missing_evidence_count\" : 0,\n    \"must_fix_count\" : 0,\n    \"acceptance_note_count\" : 0,\n    \"open_risk_count\" : 2\n  },\n  \"authored_context\" : {\n    \"sha256\" : \"9569b79f787f189c0b5d136ed02ae2e34905bd9c02036bd9a3327f59095db93d\",\n    \"ref\" : \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261023T005431Z-9YYF/runs/run-1792718401135/prompts/design-claude.md.manifest.json\"\n  }\n}\n\n\n## Active obligations\n\n[ {\n  \"id\" : \"sha256:ad1cb016896cb7cc87e8c05be6ee5ca5080ac1efb551cb458a3bfa83504a1e05#must_fix:0\",\n  \"source\" : {\n    \"ref\" : \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261023T005431Z-9YYF/runs/run-1792718638529/outputs/design-codex-review.contract.json\",\n    \"sha256\" : \"ad1cb016896cb7cc87e8c05be6ee5ca5080ac1efb551cb458a3bfa83504a1e05\"\n  },\n  \"text\" : \"AR-1：依据 AC-1 与 C-1，将共享 CASES 中 \\\"a\\\\r\\\\nb\\\\rc\\\\nd\\\" 的期望修正为 \\\"a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\nd\\\"；同步核对设计说明、test_mixed_newlines_normalized 与 README 的同一案例，避免错误期望推动实现增加空行。\"\n}, {\n  \"id\" : \"sha256:ad1cb016896cb7cc87e8c05be6ee5ca5080ac1efb551cb458a3bfa83504a1e05#must_fix:1\",\n  \"source\" : {\n    \"ref\" : \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261023T005431Z-9YYF/runs/run-1792718638529/outputs/design-codex-review.contract.json\",\n    \"sha256\" : \"ad1cb016896cb7cc87e8c05be6ee5ca5080ac1efb551cb458a3bfa83504a1e05\"\n  },\n  \"text\" : \"AR-2：依据 AC-2 与 TR-2，将测试取证方案明确为保留 stdout 和 stderr，或通过 2>&1 合并采集；保留实际逐用例结果、Ran N tests 和最终成功或失败报告，并与源码案例核对，不能只保存 stdout 或写入预期成功文本。\"\n} ]"}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"6979ff59-6b3e-40ea-aaf3-611d1dc9985c","update":{"sessionUpdate":"available_commands_update","availableCommands":[{"name":"deep-research","description":"Deep research harness — fan-out web searches, fetch sources, adversarially verify claims, synthesize a cited report. (dynamic workflow)","input":null},{"name":"design-sync","description":"Push a React design system to claude.ai/design. This runs a converter that bundles the real component code (from Storybook or a bare package) and uploads it. Use when the user runs /design-sync or says \"sync my design system to Claude Design\".","input":{"hint":"[<project hint, e.g. \"Acme DS\">]"}},{"name":"dataviz","description":"Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \"chart\", \"graph\", \"plot\", \"data viz\", \"visualization\", \"dashboard\", \"analytics\", \"visualize data\", \"categorical colors\", \"sequential / diverging palette\", \"stat tile\", \"sparkline\", \"heatmap\", \"legend\", \"axis\", \"tooltip\", \"chart colors\", \"color by series\".","input":null},{"name":"update-config","description":"Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.","input":null},{"name":"verify","description":"Verify that a code change actually does what it's supposed to by exercising it end-to-end and observing behavior — drive the affected flow, not just tests or typecheck. Run before committing nontrivial changes; bootstraps this repo's project verify skill if none exists yet. Don't invoke it on a diff that only touches tests, docs, or other code with no runtime surface to drive (a change to product source always has one) — there's nothing to observe.","input":null},{"name":"debug","description":"Enable debug logging for this session and help diagnose issues","input":{"hint":"[issue description]"}},{"name":"code-review","description":"Review the current diff, or a PR number/branch/path target, for correctness bugs and reuse/simplification/efficiency cleanups at the given effort level (low/medium: fewer, high-confidence findings; high→max: broader coverage, may include uncertain findings); with no level given, it reuses the level you typed last. Pass --comment to post findings as inline PR comments, or --fix to apply the findings to the working tree after the review.","input":{"hint":"[low|medium|high|xhigh|max] [--fix] [--comment] [<pr#>|<branch>|<path>]"}},{"name":"simplify","description":"Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.","input":{"hint":"[<target>]"}},{"name":"batch","description":"Research and plan a large-scale change, then execute it in parallel across 5–30 isolated worktree agents that each open a PR.","input":{"hint":"<instruction>"}},{"name":"fewer-permission-prompts","description":"Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.","input":null},{"name":"loop","description":"Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace.","input":{"hint":"[interval] [prompt]"}},{"name":"claude-api","description":"Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \"looks like a one-liner\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/computer-use; generate/summarize/extract/classify/rewrite/converse over NL; debugging refusals/cutoffs/streaming/tool-calls/tokens).\nSKIP only when another provider is being worked on (overrides all triggers): OpenAI/GPT/Gemini/Llama/Mistral/Cohere/Ollama named in the query; OR `grep -rE 'openai|langchain_openai|google.generativeai|genai|mistralai|cohere|ollama'` over the project hits (run this grep FIRST if no provider named — don't Read the file).","input":null},{"name":"run","description":"Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).","input":null},{"name":"run-skill-generator","description":"Author or improve the run-<unit> skill — a per-project skill that tells agents how to build, launch, and drive this project's app. Use when the user asks to set up the project, get it running, write run instructions, or verify build/run steps work from a clean environment.","input":null},{"name":"agents","description":"(removed) Ask Claude to create/manage subagents, or edit .claude/agents/","input":null},{"name":"auto-mode-setup","description":"Set up and customise auto mode — environment context, plus optional rule tweaks","input":{"hint":"[--request-id <uuid>] (--wizard posture=… scope=… depth=… --propose | --expect-sha256 <64-hex> --apply-file <path>)"}},{"name":"autocompact","description":"Configure the auto-compact window size","input":{"hint":"[auto|<tokens>]"}},{"name":"compact","description":"Free up context by summarizing the conversation so far","input":{"hint":"<optional custom summarization instructions>"}},{"name":"config","description":"Set a setting by key","input":{"hint":"key=value"}},{"name":"context","description":"Show current context usage","input":null},{"name":"effort","description":"Set effort level for model usage","input":{"hint":"<low|medium|high|xhigh|max|ultracode|auto>"}},{"name":"fast","description":"Toggle fast mode (Opus 5)","input":{"hint":"[on|off]"}},{"name":"heapdump","description":"Dump the JS heap to ~/Desktop","input":null},{"name":"init","description":"Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation","input":null},{"name":"mcp","description":"Manage MCP servers","input":{"hint":"[reconnect|enable|disable [<server>|all]]"}},{"name":"import","description":"Import config from another AI coding agent","input":null},{"name":"model","description":"Set the AI model for Claude Code","input":{"hint":"<model>"}},{"name":"__remote-workflow","description":"Run the workflow script delivered in this session environment (server-launched sessions only)","input":null},{"name":"workflow-launch-exec","description":"Execute a server-launched workflow handoff (workflow_launch event sessions only)","input":null},{"name":"reload-skills","description":"Pick up skills added or changed on disk during this session","input":null},{"name":"rename","description":"Rename the current conversation","input":{"hint":"[name]"}},{"name":"security-review","description":"Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","input":null},{"name":"usage","description":"Show session cost, plan usage, and what's contributing to your limits","input":null},{"name":"insights","description":"Generate a report analyzing your Claude Code sessions","input":null},{"name":"recap","description":"Generate a one-line session recap now","input":null},{"name":"skill-doctor","description":"Show which loaded skills are unused and costing context","input":null},{"name":"goal","description":"Set a goal — keep working until the condition is met","input":null},{"name":"design","description":"Grant or revoke Claude agent access to your Design projects","input":{"hint":"consent | revoke"}},{"name":"design-consent","description":"Grant Claude agent access to your Design projects","input":null},{"name":"design-revoke","description":"Revoke Claude agent access to your Design projects","input":null},{"name":"list-agents","description":"List subagents and other Claude sessions you can message","input":null},{"name":"team-onboarding","description":"Help teammates ramp on Claude Code with a guide from your usage","input":null}]}}}
